{
  "description": "#5691 G2b — `get_page_buffer` and `apply_page_source` with `dialect: \"document\"`: a plain block is its own paragraph, a list block carries its marker, a task is `- [ ] x`, a plain block under a list block is a `+` item, an empty block a `\\` line, a block's property lines sit at its text's column, and a heading, a fence and a break are blocks of their own. The page's own Document buffer, read by the ids beside its lines, saves as nothing, and one changed line edits its block. A save writes what the lines say beside the text: a restyled marker, a ticked or removed checkbox (a task's hidden list style going with the edit), a property line changed, emptied or added, and the marker and property lines of a line that creates a block; a value its definition refuses, or a ref line naming no page, refuses the whole save. A stale buffer merged with the page's changes keeps both versions of a block both sides changed, its text or one property, the buffer's a new block with its marker and property lines; a block one side deleted and the other changed comes back. Seed: S1 (Home) > S2 (a heading), S3 (a fence), S4 (a break), S5 (a bullet) > S6 (a plain child), S7 (numbered), S8 (a task hiding a bullet style), S9 (empty), S10 (a priority and a property), S11 (a bullet), and the definitions `count` (a number), `flag` (a boolean), `deadline` (a date) and `owner` (a ref). The query reads the Document buffer the steps left. Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` / `expected_queries` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
